/-!
# Compatible Borel and natural-module identifications in the exchanged cases

The rank-one and actual Ω₄⁺ Borels are Sylow-two normalizers. Sylow conjugacy
aligns any established natural-module identification with the source Borel,
while the same element adjusts the linear intertwiner. The orthogonal branch
constructs the required second-factor Weyl change in determinant coordinates.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, E.2.2, printed pp.215–216; F.9.18(5), pp.325–326;
and the exchanged branches in the proof of 15.3.65, printed p.1152.
Module recognition and the remaining F.9.18 filtering belong to the consumer.
-/
